  },
  "what_this_does_not_show": [
    "one machine, one client per row; the doses are bursts of abandoned calls, not a steady concurrent load",
    "a retrying client only: the desktop path (Rust engine/sidecar.rs) treats any non-200 as 'no answer' and does not retry, so its cost is the 'calls_a_non_retrying_client_loses' column, not the seconds",
    "absolute latency certification; only the comparison between settings is claimed",
    "the CT2/Argos backend, which decodes faster per call and may change where a gate starts to pay",
    "the doses are bursts of abandoned calls at one instant; a long batch that abandons a steady single call every few minutes is a different shape and would need its own run"
  ]
}
